Z||000000||qwikgta||04-23-2001||09:05 AM||||Can you post info on your targa top.. I would like to do it also...<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||10
Z||000001||Cozmo||04-23-2001||09:42 AM||||Here's some pics, Rob... <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1247137&a=9215244" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1247137&a=9215244</A>  <P>I believe the conversion was done by Corson. Haven't been able to really verify this, tho.  The top is a fiberglass shell with pins on the front and snap latches on the back edge.  The car has a box frame welded under it with a removable x section for access to the fuel tank.  I think the framing is similiar to what is used on convertible conversions.  Some members of our club are thinking of taking some molds of the top parts and duplicating them.  <BR>If you have any questions or need some better pics LMK, I'll be glad to help.<BR>Good Luck!<BR><P>------------------<BR><B>C02M0</B><BR><I>Suncoast Fieros</I><BR>'85 silver 2M6 4spd. Targa <B>"Silver Streak"</B><BR>'86 black auto GT <B>"Blackbird"</B><BR>'87 white auto Coupe <B>"The Duke"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||04-23-2001||10:27 AM||||The kit used to be sold by Corson (PISA). I called and asked about it, about a year ago. Unfortunately, it's been out of production for about three years.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
